   "read_on": "2026-10-26",
   "how_read": "Public Gallup PDFs, saved and converted with pdftotext -layout, then parsed by a script and checked. Totals: the Q8 trend table of the April 2026 topline (Oct 2001 to Apr 2026, 43 readings), printed 'Getting better' percentages; the 2017, 2019, 2020 (Apr and Jun), 2021-2025 toplines print identical figures for every reading they share (checked). The trend includes monthly readings in 2001-2003, Oct 2011 and May-Jun 2020; the target is the April survey, and non-April readings are marked in 'note'. Cells: the 'Public Release Data' crosstab of the same question in the 2019, 2020 (Apr and May-Jun) and 2021-2026 toplines, printed percentages; each crosstab's Total equals the trend figure (checked). The 2017 topline has no crosstab; no 2018 topline was found. Only Male, Female, Some College and White are kept as cells. 'White' (Gallup's Race I banner) is mapped to race_eth=white_nh by inference: these PDFs do not define Race I, but the 2025 June Confidence topline prints the White crosstab group's figures under 'Non-Hispanic White adults' (https://news.gallup.com/file/poll/692660/2025_07_17_Confidence%20in%20Institutions%20Topline%20and%20Tabs.pdf). 'published' is the date of the Gallup article that first reports the figure (read on the article page; for 2025 the 2025-04-21 economy article preceded the 2025-04-30 personal-finance article), null where none was found or read. 'Same (vol.)' and No opinion are not rescaled."
  }
